story-today = today
story-step = Step { $n } of { $total }

story-1-title = She asks, once.
story-1-text = On Telegram, the evening before. Nestor answers in the same breath and creates a **watch**: an owner, a source (her mailbox), keywords and an end.
story-1-quote = Let me know when my Vinted parcel reaches the pickup point.
story-1-reply = I’m watching your inbox: I’ll tell you as soon as it’s available.

story-2-title = The watch outlives the conversation.
story-2-text = The chat is over; the commitment isn’t. A watch is written to the journal and survives restarts, model changes and nights. It doesn’t need anyone to keep a tab open.

story-3-title = The mail arrives.
story-3-text = Her mailbox, connected over IMAP from the admin, brings in a message from the carrier. It’s a candidate, nothing more yet.
story-3-mail-subject = Your parcel is available
story-3-mail-detail = Mondial Relay: parcel available at Tabac de la Place until 6 Nov.

story-4-title = Triage, from cheap to costly.
story-4-text = Deterministic rules first, then a small classification model, and the central agent only for what deserves words. **Most events stop at the first stage.**
story-4-rules = Rules
story-4-rules-out = keywords match
story-4-model = Small model
story-4-model-out = relevant to Léa · not urgent
story-4-agent = Central agent
story-4-agent-out = words the message

story-5-title = Presence decides where.
story-5-text = Home Assistant says Léa is in the living room. No quiet hours, no conversation under way: the decision is to say it aloud, on the satellite in that room — and its reason is written down.
story-5-reason = Léa is in the “salon” room

story-6-title = Nestor says it in the living room.
story-6-text = The Reachy Mini in the living room speaks; its antennas follow the voice. The message is short, because it is said aloud in a shared room.
story-6-quote = Léa, your Vinted parcel is waiting at Tabac de la Place.

story-7-title = No reaction? A written follow-up.
story-7-text = Léa left before answering. Thirty minutes without a reply, and she is no longer home: Nestor writes to her on Telegram instead of repeating itself to an empty room.
story-7-reason = no reply for 30 min, and Léa is not home
story-7-quote = Your parcel is at Tabac de la Place until 6 November.

story-8-title = She answers. The thread holds.
story-8-text = Her reply lands with the watch’s context: Nestor knows what “it” is. And every step — trigger, triage, decision, delivery — is in the journal with its reason.
story-8-quote = Thanks! I’ll pick it up on my way home.
story-8-reply = Perfect. I’ll keep the watch open until it’s collected.
story-8-link = Why did it speak to me?

